     "page": 1,
     "text": "Monroe-Anderson Medical Group\n\nDear Colleague,\n\nI am writing to provide a comprehensive assessment of Kathy Douglas, who was seen in consultation on September 14, 2025. \n\nKathy is a 48-year-old female with several medical conditions that we have been managing in our practice. \n\n**Factor V Leiden mutation:** Kathy has a documented history of Factor V Leiden mutation, which was confirmed to be associated with venous thromboembolism (VTE). Currently, her condition is well-controlled, and she is not on any specific medications for this particular condition.\n\n**Atrial fibrillation / flutter:** Kathy was diagnosed with paroxysmal atrial fibrillation/flutter in September 2024. Echocardiographic evaluation revealed normal structural heart findings, and she has a CHADS2-VASc score of 1. Notably, an ablation procedure was performed 0.6 years ago, and she has been stable for the past 1.7 years. Kathy is currently taking diltiazem 180 mg, which has effectively controlled her atrial fibrillation.\n\n**Contraception:** Kathy's contraception plan is well-managed. She is using a of norethindrone-ethinyl estradiol 1/20 and a levonorgestrel intrauterine device (IUD) with a dosage of 52 mg. Her contraception method is currently effective, and she has no complaints related to this.\n\n**Rosacea:** Kathy has rosacea, which she has been managing with metronidazole topical 1%. Her skin condition is well-controlled, and she has not reported any recent flare-ups.\n\nOn the day of her last visit on September 14, 2025, Kathy presented for a follow-up concerning her Factor V Leiden mutation. During this visit, her blood pressure was recorded at 139/89 mmHg, and her weight was 138 pounds. The physical examination revealed no significant abnormalities. Kathy also reported no other major complaints, aside from her routine follow-up concerns.\n\n**Impression and Recommendations:**\nOverall, Kathy's medical conditions are stable and well-managed with the current treatment plans. She continues to follow up regularly to ensure her conditions remain controlled. The medications prescribed for her atrial fibrillation, contraception, and rosacea have been effective. She reports no significant side effects from her current medications.\n\nI appreciate your collaboration in managing Kathy's healthcare. Please do not hesitate to contact me if you have any further questions or require additional information.\n\nSincerely,\n\nDr. Lauren Jones \nFamily Medicine Specialist \nMonroe-Anderson Medical Group\n\n**Social History:** \nKathy reports consuming approximately 10 alcoholic drinks per week. \n\n---\n\nT"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "his letter should serve as a thorough summary of Kathy's medical status and ongoing management plan.\n"
